@@s001 Code: vertex cover by brute force
@@s002 Code: vertex cover by brute force
@@s003 All the subsets of nodes, encoded as the bits of an integer, with the edge check and the bit count with bitCount.
@@s004 Subsets as bits
@@s005 The number <code>k</code> from 0 to 2ⁿ − 1 represents a subset: bit i says whether node i is chosen.
@@s006 Subsets as bits
@@s007 <code>1 &lt;&lt; n</code> is 2ⁿ: the loop goes through all the subsets.
@@s008 I extract the bit of node u: I shift <code>k</code> to the right and isolate the last bit with <code>&amp; 1</code>.
@@s009 Every edge must have at least one endpoint chosen: otherwise this subset is not a cover.
@@s010 The number of bits set is the size of the subset: I compare it with the best.
@@s011 Syntax notes
@@s012 <code>&gt;&gt;</code> is the right shift, <code>&amp;</code> is the bitwise AND, <code>&lt;&lt;</code> is the left shift.
@@s013 Cost <code>O(2ⁿ · m)</code>: exponential, but correct for small n.
@@s014 Running it
@@s015 Example of input and output (actually compiled and run).
